  "id": "behavioral-contingency",
  "term": "behavioral contingency",
  "definition": "Behavioral contingency is the link between what a person does or withholds doing and the outcome that follows, such as reward or punishment. In this source, it refers to whether a go or no-go response, and whether it is correct or incorrect, leads to winning or losing.",
